#92000
"Narrow Ledge over the Inner Sea"
"You are on a narrow lip of rock far above the pounding surf of the Inner Sea.

This ledge is only a few feet across and would be impossible to see from

above.  It hugs the steep cliff wall to the east and drops away sharply to the

distant waters below.  The ledge is impossible to follow south, but to the

north it slants down steeply and winds around a small outcropping.

"
