#92003
"Before the Gates"
"A towering stone wall cuts off this narrow strip of land from the rest of the

island.  From this angle it is impossible to see what might lie on the other

side of the wall save what you can see through the open gates.  Directly above

the gates are crenalated battlements, ready to repel any unwelcome visitors. 

South of here is a massive wooden bridge that spans the choppy waters of the

sea below.

"
